352,353,356,357,360,361,363,364,367,368,371,372,374,375,377],{},"Without a local ",[303,343,182],{},", ",[303,346,347],{},"file-name"," is shown. The download button appears only when a ",[303,350,351],{},"download"," function is passed, and it is called only when the button is pressed, so there is no need to fetch the file up front and put it in ",[303,354,355],{},"v-model","; the page decides on auth headers, POST and the like. Return a ",[303,358,359],{},"Blob"," to have the component save it under ",[303,362,347],{},", or return nothing if the page handled the download itself (for example by opening a new tab). While downloading, the button shows a spinner and ignores repeated clicks; throwing an error shows the download failed toast (requires ",[303,365,366],{},"UApp","), and the passed ",[303,369,370],{},"signal"," is aborted on unmount. With a local ",[303,373,182],{},", the local file is downloaded directly and ",[303,376,351],{}," is not called.",[300,379,380,381,385],{},"When the file name is truncated, hovering or keyboard focus shows the full name, or a long press on touch devices (see ",[382,383,217],"a",{"href":384},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Fhelper\u002Ftooltip#touch-long-press","); a long press does not open the file dialog.",[332,387],{"name":388},"file-existing",[313,390,392],{"id":391},"clearing","Clearing",[300,394,395,398,399,401,402,404,405,407,408,404,410,413,414,417,418,420],{},[303,396,397],{},"clear"," is on by default and shows a trailing clear button when there is a local ",[303,400,182],{}," or an existing attachment; it is hidden while disabled or loading. Clearing sets ",[303,403,355],{}," to ",[303,406,325],{}," and ",[303,409,347],{},[303,411,412],{},"''",", leaving the field completely empty so a new file can be selected. Bind the attachment name with ",[303,415,416],{},"v-model:file-name"," so the page can tell from ",[303,419,412],{}," that the user removed the existing attachment; when it is passed one-way, clearing still empties the